  "script_defect_found": {
    "summary": "check_archive() assumed digests.lock's image_id (docker inspect .Id at collection time) always equals the docker-save archive's manifest.json Config digest. Under Docker Desktop's containerd-backed image store (default since 4.34, active on this machine), .Id returns the pulled manifest(-list) digest instead.",
    "first_fix_bypassable": "The first fix (e151d11) accepted any index.json manifest digest whose blob re-hashed correctly, but nothing linked that blob to the manifest.json Config/Layers syft actually scans; an approval review's PoC tar (real index bytes + unrelated manifest.json/config) was accepted. The classic path also never checked layer tars against the config's rootfs.diff_ids.",
    "fix": "scripts/airgap/archive_identity.py check_archive(): every manifest.json layer is re-hashed (stored bytes, and gzip-decompressed stream) and must equal config rootfs.diff_ids in order; if the lock digest is the config digest that is the whole binding (classic). Otherwise the lock digest must be a blob in the archive that re-hashes to its name; a manifest list selects exactly one linux/arm64 entry (ambiguity rejected), that manifest blob is re-hashed, its config.digest must equal the re-hashed manifest.json Config and its layers[].digest must equal the re-hashed manifest.json Layers blobs in order. index.json is never consulted. Tar members with traversal, links, or duplicate names are rejected.",
    "regression_tests_added": "scripts/airgap/test_archive_identity.py (run by test_sbom.sh): 5 genuine chains accepted, 15 forged/malformed archives rejected (reviewer PoC, swapped/reordered layers, rewritten config, mismatched config, two linux/arm64 manifests, missing list/manifest/layer blob, manifest blob not hashing to its name, unrelated lock digest, classic layer swap, path traversal, symlink, duplicate manifest.json).",
    "trace": ".agents/evals/traces/2026-09-issue-98-sbom-containerd-store.json"
  },
